Today I completed the following coding challenge:

The Goal:
Given an array of objects, each with a "name" and "age" property, return an array 
containing the names of the oldest people. If multiple people share the maximum age, 
return all of their names in the order they appear in the input.

My Approach:
 1.First, I checked if the list was empty to handle edge cases safely.
 2.I declared a variable called max_age to store the highest age found in the list using a 
   generator expression.
 3.Finally, I used a list comprehension to filter and return the names of all individuals whose age matches the max_age. 
   This ensures the original order is preserved.

